---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Process-Based Music Therapy — That Music Therapy Lot | Music Therapy & SEND Consultation in Walthamstow"
  description="Process-Based Music Therapy in London and Waltham Forest, E17. An HCPC-regulated creative space for trauma, SEMH, and change — specialists in Process-Based Music Therapy when words aren’t enough."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="section__eyebrow reveal">Therapy for you</p>
      <h1 class="page-hero__title reveal">Your experiences are unique; your therapy should be too.</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lede reveal">
        Process-based music therapy — a creative space to explore feelings when
        words might fail or escape us.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="section section--tight" style="padding-top: 0;">
      <figure class="page-visual reveal">
        <img
          src="/images/web/GuitarSoundBowl.jpg"
          alt="Close-up of a classical guitar soundhole and strings"
          width="2400"
          height="1350"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>

    <section class="section section--tight">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="prose reveal">
          <h2>The creative space</h2>
          <p>
            Music therapy is a form of psychotherapy, primarily non-linguistic,
            and a powerful place to explore feelings when words aren’t enough.
            The “process-based” part means we aren’t chasing a fixed playlist of
            techniques — we attend to what is actually happening between you,
            the music, and the relationship, moment by moment.
          </p>
          <p>
            This is a space to begin embodying new experiences, develop new ways
            of relating to trauma, and try defusion and psychological flexibility
            work in a medium that can bypass the limits of talk alone.
          </p>
          <p>
            Music therapy is an HCPC-registered profession: only
            state-registered practitioners can use the title, with their own
            code of ethics and conduct.
          </p>

          <h2>Underpinned by RFT and ACT</h2>
          <p>
            Our clinical work is grounded in Relational Frame Theory (RFT) —
            the behavioural science of language and cognition that underpins
            Acceptance and Commitment Therapy (ACT). Music is highly relational
            and often pre-verbal; bringing RFT into the music therapy space
            helps us work with stuck patterns without relying only on narrative.
          </p>
          <p>
            ACT doesn’t aim to erase difficult feelings. It builds psychological
            flexibility — the capacity to stay present, loosen the grip of
            unhelpful stories, and move toward what matters. In sessions that
            can look like improvisation, songwriting, listening, and structured
            musical tasks that map onto core ACT processes:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Present-moment awareness</strong> — musical engagement as
              an anchor in the here and now
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Cognitive defusion</strong> — using sound and lyric to
              externalise and untangle from sticky thoughts
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Values and committed action</strong> — exploring musical
              identity and expression to clarify what matters, and take steps
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Looking for talking therapy?</h2>
          <p>
            Integrative psychotherapy now lives at
            {' '}<a href="https://therapywithben.uk/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Therapy With Ben</a>
            — a dedicated space for that work. This site is focused on
            process-based music therapy, consulting, and measurement.
          </p>

          <p>
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/#contact">Get in touch</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="aside-note reveal" aria-label="Professional standards">
          <h3>Professional standards</h3>
          <p>
            Music Therapist is a protected title in the UK. Practitioners at
            That Music Therapy Lot maintain HCPC registration and ongoing CPD.
          </p>
          <ul class="trust-list">
            <li><a href="https://www.hcpc-uk.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">HCPC</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.bamt.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">BAMT</a></li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
